<div class="tldr"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> the best Vermont ski resorts for families are Smugglers' Notch for kids' programs and child care, Okemo for young beginners, Stratton for a polished village, Jay Peak for its indoor waterpark, Stowe for a classic ski town, and Killington and Sugarbush for mixed-ability groups. On a budget, Bolton Valley, Magic Mountain and Mad River Glen are smaller and more relaxed.</p></div>

