<h2>Vermont tips for families</h2>
<h3>Dress for cold and ice</h3>
<p>Vermont winters are cold, and January days below zero with wind chill are common. Freeze-thaw cycles can leave trails firm and icy. Pack face masks, hand warmers and extra layers, take frequent lodge breaks with small kids, and keep edges sharp. Consider shorter ski days in midwinter and plan for softer snow in March.</p>
<h3>Know your interstate: I-89 or I-91</h3>
<p>I-89 runs through northern Vermont and is the way to Stowe, Smugglers' Notch, Bolton Valley, Sugarbush and Mad River Glen, with Burlington (BTV) the closest airport. I-91 runs up the eastern edge and serves Okemo, Stratton, Magic Mountain and, much farther north, Jay Peak. Killington is reached on US-4. In winter, Route 108 through Smugglers' Notch closes between Stowe and Smuggs, so don't plan on driving over the notch.</p>
<h3>Use family programs and the Fifth Grade Passport</h3>
<p>Smugglers' Notch is the standout for family programs: Treasures child care takes babies from 6 weeks old, and Snow Sport University runs lessons and camps for kids and teens. Book childcare and lessons when you book lodging. Ski Vermont's Fifth Grade Passport gives fifth graders from any state free days at participating Vermont areas when they ski with a paying adult; check the current fee and holiday restrictions.</p>
<h3>Pick your month</h3>
<p>Most Vermont resorts are at their best from mid-January through mid-March, when the base is deepest. Each resort's "best time to ski" page shows its snowiest months, for example <%= link_to "best time to ski Stowe", best_time_resort_path("stowe") %>. The <%= link_to "Vermont snow report", region_path("vermont") %> ranks every resort on this week's forecast.</p>

<h2>Next steps</h2>
<p>Read <%= link_to "how to choose a family ski resort", guide_path("best-family-ski-resorts") %> and <%= link_to "skiing with kids by age", guide_path("skiing-with-kids") %>, check <%= link_to "kids' ski gear and sizing", guide_path("kids-ski-gear") %>, then use the free <%= link_to "Ski Trip Planner", ski_trip_planner_path %> to plan the timeline and budget.</p>
